**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The import seam lists the user's entries and pins a version of any kind, which every export needs (001 §B 'Export: … Exporting pins the exported versions (§C)'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned — a one-way flag — when a kit first references it, or when it is exported'; the S3.3 brief: exporting pins every exported version through S2.2's pin verbs). S2.2's verbs (`pinMaterialVersion`, `pinSampleVersion`, step 65) cover two kinds, and the source, preset and category stores have none (S2.3 interpretation 4). So the kind-neutral pin lives on the envelope seam (step 94), and its database half shares one body with those verbs. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportProxy` gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `heldUserEntries : unit -> Result<HeldEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers every held entry whose latest provenance is not a built-in (`provenance.protection` is `UserManaged`: user, kit-import, pulled and forked entries), whatever its lifecycle, each as `tryHeldEntry` answers it. `pinEntryVersion : LibraryEntryId -> VersionNumber -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` pins one held version, one way. It answers `Ok ()` also when the version is already pinned, and `ImportRejectedErr` naming the id and the version when that version is not held. The record's doc names both in no more words. (2) The in-memory double (`createInMemory`, step 95). `heldUserEntries` answers the map's entries whose latest provenance is `UserManaged`, in the map's id order. `pinEntryVersion` answers `ImportRejectedErr` for a version the map does not hold. For a held material or sample version it decodes the envelope (step 25), as its put does, and calls the bundled store's `pinMaterialVersion` or `pinSampleVersion` (step 65); a refusal is `ImportRejectedErr` with the store's reason. For every other kind it answers `Ok ()`, because the in-memory category, source and preset stores hold no pin. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`: the operations' extension (step 67) gains `stagePin (id : LibraryEntryId) (version : VersionNumber) : Result<StoredEntryVersion option, StorageError>` under the same `StorageBoundary` mark. It calls `tryStoredVersion id version`; a held version is restaged through `stageVersion` with `pin = VersionPinned` and its lifecycle kept, and is answered as it was found; a version not held answers `None`. It stages and never saves. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs`' `pinMaterialVersion` (step 69) and `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs`' `pinSampleVersion` (step 74) call it in place of their own restage and keep their refusals, so one body pins a version row. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`' `createInDatabase` (step 95). `heldUserEntries` answers, in one `database.run` and as `heldEntriesOf` does, every entry whose latest row (`LatestVersion` joined to `EntryVersion`) has `Protection` = `UserManaged.value`, in no promised order. `pinEntryVersion id version` is one `run` of `stagePin` and one `SaveChanges ()`; `None` is `ImportRejectedErr` naming the id and the version. Every `StorageError` is `ImportStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`, as for its other fields. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs`: `recordingProxy` (step 94) answers `heldUserEntries` with `[]` and `pinEntryVersion` with `Ok ()`. No cache, retry, unpin verb or other field is added: a pin is one-way (001 §C). (6) Tests. `CatalogueImportContract` gains two facts, so each runs over both stores; their entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `putSealedEntries` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. `heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in`: before any put it answers `[]`. After `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass`, `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` and a fork of `PTB glass` (as step 114's fact builds it) are put, and `Lab glass` is retired through `retireEntry`, it answers exactly those three ids, compared as a set, each with its own name. `pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held`: `Lab glass`'s version 1 is pinned through `pinEntryVersion`, and a second pin of it answers `Ok ()`. The material, decoded and given the catalogue Langasite's complexity, saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial` then resolves at versions 1 and 2, and version 1 keeps Silicon's complexity. A put `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack`, its version 1 pinned the same way, makes `samples.removeSample` answer `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. Version 3 of `Lab glass` and version 1 of a test-local GUID answer `ImportRejectedErr`. `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` gains `pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle`. Over a database the fact opens as the class's `freshImport` does, after `importFrom` of the Built-in catalogue and `retireEntry` of one built-in source, `pinEntryVersion` of version 1 of one entry of each of the six kinds, that source included, leaves each of those rows `VersionPinned`, read through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`. The source stays `InactiveEntry`, and every other entry's version 1 stays `VersionUnpinned`. The inherited `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` and `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` (steps 66, 73) run unchanged over the shared `stagePin`.

**Acceptance.** After the seam grows, both implementations of `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST answer `heldUserEntries` and `pinEntryVersion`, and the database pin verbs MUST share `stagePin`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in` and `pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held` over both stores and `pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.
